      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/ATDS/86.1\npage 3\n\nGUIDELINES FOR THE PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF INFECTION\nWITH LAV/HTLV-II1\n\n1. Introduction\n\n-An important component of the WHO AIDS Control Programme (ACP) is\n\npreparation and distribution of guidelines, manuals and educational materials\n\non prevention and control of LAV/HTLV-III infections for professional\n\npersonnel, for groups at risk and for the general public. The ultimate goal\n\nof the ACP guidelines is prevention of LAV/HTLV-III transmission, using\n\nstrategies firmly anchored in fundamental public health concepts and utilizing\n\nthe best available knowledge on the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the guidelines as part of the WHO AIDS Control Programme, aimed at public health authorities and health professionals who must adapt them to local settings, and notes they will be revised as knowledge grows. It describes the virus and states that only blood and semen have been implicated in transmission, through sexual, parenteral and perinatal routes.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
