      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/page-008.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/AIDS/86,1\npage 6\n\n- absence of all known underlying causes of cellular immunodeficiency\nCother than LAV/HTLV-III infection) and absence of a11 other causes of\n\nreduced resistance reported to be associated with at least one of those\nopportunistic diseases.\n\nDespite having the above, patients are excluded as AIDS cases if they have\nnegative result(s) on testing for serum antibody to LAV/HTLV-IIT, do not have\na positive culture for LAV/HTLV-I11, and have both a normal or high number of\nT-helper (OKT4 or LEU3) lymphocytes and a normal or high ratio of T-helper to\nT-suppressors (OKT8 or LEU",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Completes the WHO/CDC AIDS case definition, including exclusion criteria based on negative tests and normal T-helper counts. It then gives the clinical case definitions for adults and begins the definition for paediatric AIDS.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
