      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/page-009.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS /AIDS/86.1\npage 7\n\nMajor signs\nbad weight loss or abnormally slow growth;\n- chronic diarrhoea > 1 month;\n\n- prolonged fever 5 1 month,\n\nMinor signs\n- generalized lymphadenopathy;\n\n- oro-pharyngeal candidiasis;\n\n~ repeated common infections (otitis, pharyngitis, etc.)\n- persistent cough;\n\n- generalized dermatitis;\n\n- confirmed maternal LAV/HTLV-LII infection\n\nThese clinical case definitions are believed to be sensitive but have not\nyet been formally evaluated. There may be differences in clinical features\n\namong different countries, Therefore, there ig an urgent need to carefully\nevalua",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists major and minor signs for the clinical definition of paediatric AIDS and calls for evaluating clinical definitions in different settings. It opens the recommendations for health care workers, stressing avoidance of exposure to patients' blood and keeping workers with weeping lesions from direct patient contact.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
