      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/page-010.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/ATDS /86.1\npage &\n\nrequires tigorous sterilization of reusable equipment such as needles,\nsyringes and skin~plercing instruments.\n\n2.1 Precautions for HCWs\n\nThese precautions represent prudent practices that apply to preventing\ntransmission of all bloodborne infections and should be used routinely.\n\n2.4.1. Sharp items (needles, scalpel blades, and other instruments) should\nbe considered as potentially infective, should be handled with extraordinary\ncare to prevent accidental injuries, and should be placed into\npuncture-resistant containers located as close as practical to the area in\nw",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out precautions for health care workers against bloodborne infections, including careful handling and disposal of sharps without recapping, safe destruction of disposable needles and syringes, and use of gloves, gowns and masks where appropriate. It also covers handling of specimens, waste and reusable instruments, including those with lenses.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
