      "id": "library/10665-59577/blocks/prose-page-011",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 11",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/page-011.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/ATDS/86.1\npage 9\n\n2.1.6, Disposable needles and syringes are preferred. Only needle-locking\nsyringes or one-piece needle-syringe units should be used to aspirate fluids\n\nfrom patients, so that collected fluid can be safely discharged through the\nneedle, if desired, If reusable syringes are employed, they must be\n\nsterilized before reuse (see section 7.3) and special care must be taken in\nhandling to avoid injuries,\n\n2.1.7. Precautious such as single-room isolation are not generally indicated\nfor LAV/RTLV-LII infected patients. However, to the extent possible, a\nprivate room may be indi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends disposable or safely sterilized needles and syringes, explains that single-room isolation is not usually needed except in specific circumstances, and advises on resuscitation equipment. It also covers precautions for home care and pre-hospital emergency care providers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
