      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/AIDS/86,1\npage 12\n\n2.9 Eye examiners*\n\n3. Considerations relevant to non health cate workers\n\n3.1 Personal service workers\n\nPersonal service workers are defined as individuals whose occupations\ninvolve close personal contact with clients (e.g. hairdressers, barbers,\nmanicurists, pedicurists, massage therapists). Personal service workers whose\nservices (tattoolng, ear piercing, acupuncture, etc.) require needles or other\ninstruments that penetrate the skin should follow precautions indicated for\nhealth care workers, Particular care must be taken to ensure that all\nskin-piercing instrume",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Covers non-health care workers, advising that personal service workers who pierce the skin follow health worker precautions and properly disinfect instruments, though no transmission has been documented in such settings. It states that food service workers with LAV/HTLV-III need not be restricted from work unless they have other illnesses.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
