      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/CDS/AIDS/86.1\npage 14\n\n4 10 to 30 minute contact time is required depending upon level of\ncontamination of material to be disinfected.\n\n7.1.2, Formaldehyde as Formalin: 50 g/litre (5%). 10-30 minute contact time.\n\n7.143, Ethanol; 700 g/litre (702). 10-30 minute contact time,\n7.1.4, Glutaraldehyde: 20 g/litve (24). 10-30 minute contact time.\n7.2 Sterilization\n\n7.2.1 Ideally, all reusable patient care equipment and instruments entering\nthe blood stream or tissue should be sterilized by steam under pressure\n(autoclaving), Autoclaves should be operated at 121°C (250°F) for a\n\nminimum exposure",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives contact times for disinfectants such as formalin, ethanol and glutaraldehyde, and describes sterilization by autoclaving or boiling and high-level disinfection of heat-sensitive equipment. It sets out a step-by-step method for processing reusable needles and syringes.",
